===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|fon|lang=enm}}, {{term|fonne|lang=enm}}, of {{etyl|gmq|en}} origin, related to {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|fåne||a fool, idiot, prat|lang=sv}} (compare {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|fånig||foolish|lang=sv}}), {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|fáni||a buoyant, high-flying person|lit=a standard, flag|lang=is}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*fanô||cloth, rag}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*pān-||fabric}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|fana||a banner, standard|lang=ang}}. More at {{l|en|vane}}. 

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} A [[fool]] or [[idiot]].

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|fonner}}

# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} [[foolish|Foolish]]; [[simple]]; [[silly]].

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|fonnen|lang=enm}}, from {{term|fon|lang=enm}}, {{term|fonne||fool|lang=enm}}. 

====Verb====
{{en-verb|fonn|ing}}

# {{context|intransitive|obsolete|lang=en}} To be foolish or simple; act like a fool; [[dote]].

===Etymology 3===

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[chieftain]] or [[king]] of a region of [[Cameroon]].

